<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ugandan Bush War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1981">1981</a>–<a href="/years/1986">1986</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Luwero War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ugandan Bush War was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war waged by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoweri-museveni">Yoweri Museveni</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-resistance-army">National Resistance Army</a> against the second government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-obote">Milton Obote</a> and then the military regime of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tito-okello">Tito Okello</a>. Fighting centred on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luwero-triangle">Luwero Triangle</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kampala">Kampala</a>, where many civilians were killed. The NRA took Kampala in January 1986 and Museveni became president.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ugandan-bush-war.jpg" alt="Ugandan Bush War" width="216" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Helmut Schaar · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Obote_cropped.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
